# Cursor AI Rules — Knowledge Portal

## Project Context
Enterprise knowledge management system: Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, TypeScript strict, SQLite via @libsql/client, Drizzle ORM, NextAuth v5 beta (JWT), Qdrant vector DB, Ollama LLM, TipTap editor, Tailwind CSS v4.

## Critical Rules

### Database (Drizzle + libsql)
- ALL queries are async. Always `await`.
- Single result: `const user = await db.select()...get();` (returns `T | undefined`)
- Multiple results: `const items = await db.select()...all();` (returns `T[]`)
- Alternative single: `const [user] = await db.select()...limit(1);`
- NEVER omit `await` — queries return Promises.
- NEVER use `better-sqlite3` or any native SQLite binding.
- Schema is in `src/lib/db/schema.ts`. After changes: `npm run db:generate` → `npm run db:migrate`.

### Middleware (Edge Runtime)
- `src/middleware.ts` runs in Edge Runtime.
- CANNOT import `fs`, `path`, `crypto`, or any DB/ORM modules.
- Use `getToken` from `next-auth/jwt` with explicit `secret: process.env.NEXTAUTH_SECRET`.
- CANNOT use `auth()` from NextAuth (requires Node.js runtime).

### Authentication & RBAC
- NextAuth v5 beta with JWT strategy (no DB sessions).
- Roles: `admin`, `editor`, `viewer`.
- RBAC helpers: `src/lib/auth/rbac.ts` — `requireAuth()`, `requirePermission()`, `hasPermission()`.
- JWT token contains `id` and `role` fields (extended in `src/types/next-auth.d.ts`).

### API Routes
- Located in `src/app/api/` as Next.js Route Handlers.
- Always validate input with Zod.
- Always check auth/permissions at the top of each handler.
- Return `NextResponse.json()` — consistent shape: `{ data }` or `{ error: string }`.
- NEVER add `"use server"` to API route files.

### Components & Styling
- Use `cn()` from `src/lib/utils.ts` for conditional classNames.
- Icons from `lucide-react` only.
- TipTap editor: dynamically imported with `next/dynamic` and `ssr: false`.
- Tailwind CSS v4 utility classes only — no CSS modules, no styled-components.

### File Structure
```
src/app/[route]/page.tsx      → Page component
src/app/api/[route]/route.ts  → API handler
src/components/[domain]/      → Domain components
src/lib/[module]/             → Shared utilities
src/types/                    → TypeScript type declarations
src/workers/                  → Background processes
```

## Environment Variables
- `DATABASE_URL` — SQLite path (e.g., `./data/knowledge.db`)
- `NEXTAUTH_SECRET` — JWT signing secret (required)
- `NEXTAUTH_URL` — App base URL
- `QDRANT_URL` — Vector DB endpoint
- `OLLAMA_URL` — Ollama LLM server endpoint

## Commands
```bash
npm run dev          # Dev server (Turbopack)
npm run build        # Production build
npm run db:generate  # Generate migration from schema
npm run db:migrate   # Apply migrations
npm run db:seed      # Seed initial data (admin user)
npm run worker       # Background indexing worker
```

## Do NOT
- Use `better-sqlite3` (native compilation)
- Import Node.js built-ins (`fs`, `path`, `crypto`) in middleware
- Use synchronous DB patterns
- Add `"use server"` to API route files
- Use `auth()` in middleware
- Install additional CSS frameworks (stick to Tailwind)
- Use relative imports crossing `src/` boundary — use `@/` alias
